mode: "100644"
text: "# The Image Brief\n\nBefore any prompt: decide what image this post actually needs. A prompt with no brief produces a\npretty, purposeless picture. This is the step the tool-specific skills assume you've already done.\n\n## Start with the \"should this even be AI-generated?\" gate\n\nAI image generation is one option, not the default. Often something else wins:\n\n- **A real photo** — your actual product, space, team, or result. **Authenticity beats AI** for trust;\n  raw/real content frequently outperforms polished AI, and AI **cannot** depict your real place/people.\n- **A screenshot** — a testimonial, a result, a UI, a stat in context. Concrete and credible.\n- **UGC** — a customer's photo/video (with permission). Social proof AI can't fake.\n- **A chart/diagram** — for data, a clean chart (or a design tool) is clearer and honest.\n- **Stock** — when generic is fine and faster.\n\nReach for **AI generation** when you need something that doesn't exist, must match a specific brand\nlook, needs legible in-image text, or you want a consistent series — and a real asset isn't available.\nIf a real asset is better, **say so**; don't generate for the sake of it.\n\n## If you're generating, write the brief\n\nFour questions, answered before prompting:\n\n1. **Job / purpose.** What is this image *for*? Common social jobs:\n   - **Stop-scroll hero** — earn the pause in the feed.\n   - **Explainer / infographic** — make a concept/steps clear (verify the data).\n   - **Quote / text graphic** — a line of copy as the visual (text-led).\n   - **Product shot** — the thing itself, in context.\n   - **Lifestyle / scene** — the world around the brand.\n   - **Thumbnail** — the click (high contrast, a focal point, room for a few words).\n   - **Background / overlay base** — a backdrop for text added later.\n   - **Ad creative** — hero + offer + CTA.\n2. **The one thing it must convey.** A single idea/feeling. If it's trying to say five things, it says\n   nothing. Name the one.\n3. **Format / aspect ratio** for the destination — 1:1, 4:5 (feed portrait/carousel), 9:16 (Stories/\n   Reels/TikTok), 16:9 (thumbnail/landscape), 2:3/3:4 (Pinterest/poster). Decide up front.\n4. **Brand look.** Pull from `brand-profile.md` — palette, visual style, typographic feel, do/don't —\n   so the image looks like the brand, not generic. (Or capture it as a reference image / brand model in\n   the tool.)\n\n## Output of this step\n\nA one-line brief you can hand to a prompt: *\"[Job] for [platform, aspect ratio], conveying [the one\nthing], in [brand look].\"* From there → `prompt-anatomy.md` (describe it) → `choosing-the-tool.md`\n(pick the model).\n"
